   R_1 = 1 - (1 - R_1(t)) \times (1 - R_2(t))
   \]  
   
   The reliability of Stage 2 is:  
   \[
   R_2 = R_1 \times R_3(t) \times R_4(t)
   \]  
   
   The overall reliability of the system is:  
   \[
   R_S(t) = R_2 = (1 - (1 - R_1(t)) \times (1 - R_2(t))) \times R_3(t) \times R_4(t)
   \]  
   
   **General Approach:**  
   - Break down the system into smaller stages (series or parallel).  
   - Compute the reliability of each stage.  
