","To find the maximum height reached by the particle, we use the kinematic equations for uniformly accelerated motion. The initial velocity \( u = 20 \, \text{m/s} \), the final velocity at the maximum height \( v = 0 \, \text{m/s} \), and the acceleration due to gravity \( a = -9.8 \, \text{m/s}^2 \) (downward). The height \( h \) is the maximum height.

