2. Record the \(n\) values of \(^{147}\text{Cs}\) transfer factors.

**Step 2: Calculate the Geometric Mean**
1. Multiply all the \(n\) values of \(^{147}\text{Cs}\) transfer factors together.
2. Raise the product by the power of \(1/n\) (or take the \(n\)-th root).

**Example:**
If the \(^{147}\text{Cs}\) transfer factors are 0.01, 0.02, 0.03, and 0.04, then:
\[
\text{Geometric Mean} = \left(0.01 \times 0.02 \times 0.03 \times 0.04\right)^{1/4} = (0.000000024)^{1/4} \approx 0.00015
\]

