1. **Formation of Sulfides:**
   \[
   \text{M}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{MS} + \text{H}_2\text{O}
   \]
   where \( \text{M}^{2+} \) represents the metal ions (\( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \text{Hg}^{2+} \)).

2. **Solubility Products (\( K_{sp} \)) of Sulfides:**
   - \( \text{CuSO}_4 \) (\( \text{Cu}^{2+} \)): \( \text{CuSO}_4 \rightleftharpoons \text{Cu}^{2+} + \text{SO}_4^{2-} \), \( K_{sp} = 1.0 \times 10^{-3} \text{ M}^2 \).
   - \( \text{HgSO}_4 \) (\( \text{Hg}^{2+} \)): \( \text{HgSO}_4 \rightleftharpoons \text{Hg}^{2+} + \text{SO}_4^{2-} \), \( K_{sp} = 1.0 \times 10^{-10} \text{M}^2 \).
