The moles of \( NH_4CNO \) are \( \frac{22.9 \, \text{g}}{114.01 \, \text{g/mol}} = 0.201 \, \text{mol} \).  
The concentration of \( NH_4CNO \) is \( \frac{0.201 \, \text{mol}}{1.00 \, \text{dm}^3} = 0.201 \, \text{M} \).  

**Step 2: Calculate the change in concentration of urea at each time interval.**  
The mass of urea is given in grams, but we need the concentration.  
