The volume of the first cube is 27 units.  
The volume of a cube is given by \(V = a^3\), where \(a\) is the edge length of the cube.  
For the first cube, let its edge length be \(a_1\). Then \(a_1^3 = 27\), so \(a_1 = sqrt[3]{27} = 3\).  
For the second cube, let its edge length be \(a_2\).  
The ratio of the edges is \(\frac{a_1}{a_2} = \frac{3}{1}\), so \(a_1 = 3a_2\).  
Substituting \(a_1 = 3\), we get \(3 = 3a_2\), which implies \(a_2 = 1\).  
The volume of the second cube is \(V_2 = a_2^3 = 1^3 = 1\).  

