</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To find the fraction of kinetic energy lost during the collision, we use the coefficient of restitution \( e \). The coefficient of restitution is given by:
\[
e = \frac{v_{\text{out}}}{v_{\text{in}}}
\]
where \( v_{\text{out}} \) is the velocity of the block after the collision and \( v_{\text{in}} \) is the velocity of the ball before the collision.

Given the coefficient of restitution \( e = \frac{1}{3} \), we have:
\[
\frac{v_{\text{out}}}{v_{\text{in}}} = \frac{1}{3}
\]
Thus, the velocity after the collision is:
\[
v_{\text{out}} = \frac{1}{3} v_{\text{in}}
\]

The kinetic energy of the ball before the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{in}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2
\]
The kinetic energy of the ball after the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{out}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{out}}^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{3} v_{\text{in}} \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{9} v_{\text{in}}^2 \right) = \frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2) = \frac{1}{9} K_{\text{in}}
\]

The loss in kinetic energy is:
\[
\Delta K = K_{\text{in}} - K_{\text{out}} = K_{\text{in}} - \frac{1}{9} K_{\text{in}} = \frac{8}{9} K_{\text{in}}
\]

The fraction of kinetic energy lost is:
\[
\frac{\Delta K}{K_{\text{in}}} = \frac{\frac{8}{9} K_{\text{in}}}{K_{\text{in}}} = \frac{8}{9}
\]

Thus, the fraction of kinetic energy lost during the collision is \(\boxed{\dfrac{8}{9}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

