\[
\frac{dV}{dt} = \frac{i}{C}.
\]
Differentiating \( V(t) = 10e^{-4t} \) with respect to \( t \):
\[
\frac{dV}{dt} = -40e^{-4t}.
\]
Substituting \( \frac{dV}{dt} \) and \( i(t) \) into the differential equation:
\[
-40e^{-4t} = \frac{0.2e^{-4t}}{C}.
\]
