The index of refraction \( n \) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum \( c \) to the speed of light in a medium \( v \):
\[
n = \frac{c}{v}
\]
Given that the speed of light in the plastic is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum, the speed of light in the plastic is:
\[
v = 0.680c
\]
Substituting this into the formula for the index of refraction:
