- \( c \) is the speed of light in vacuum (\( c = 2.998 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s} \)),
- \( \lambda \) is the wavelength of the radiation,
- \( T \) is the absolute temperature of the black body in Kelvin.

This equation represents the spectral radiance of the black body, which is the power emitted per unit area, per unit wavelength.

The total power emitted per unit area (Stefan-Stefanhoffhoff law) is the integral of this over all wavelengths:
\[
