\[
\Delta S_{\text{gas}} = \frac{1858.5 \text{ kJ}}{1100 - 550} \times 1.005 \text{ kJ/kgK} = \frac{1858.5 \times 1.005}{550} \text{ J/K} = 3.4 \text{ J/K}
\]
The entropy change of the water is:
\[
\Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{1858.5 \text{ kJ}}{220 \text{ K}} = 8.42 \text{ J/K}
\]
The total entropy change is:
\[
\Delta S = \Delta S_{\text{gas}} + \Delta S_{\text{water}} = 3.4 + 8.42 = 11.82 \text{ J/K}
