","The presence of dark matter plays a significant role in the formation and evolution of black holes in the universe. It is not a direct component of black holes (dark matter is not converted into dark matter-based black holes), but it influences the conditions in which black holes can form and evolve. Here are some ways in which dark matter affects black hole formation and evolution:

