\]
The entropy change of the water is:
\[
\Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{q_{\text{water}}}{T_{\text{water}}} = \frac{m_{\text{water}} L_{\text{water}}}{T_{\text{water}}}
\]
Since all the heat transferred from the gases goes to the water, the heat lost by the gases is equal to the heat absorbed by the water:
\[
q_{\text{gas}} = q_{\text{water}}
\]
The heat absorbed by the water is:
\[
q_{\text{water}} = m_{\text{water}} L_{\text{water}} = 1 \text{ kg} \times 1858.5 \text{ kJ/kg} = 1858.5 \text{ kJ}
\]
